out+=['The returned source-citing titles identify no explicit solution of Question 9. This is a bounded, metadata-level citation screen, not a full-text review of every citing paper.','## Read-only brain and prior work','Ran math_recall.py "Brownian carousel Sine beta Painleve", brain.py recall "Brownian carousel Painleve", and brain.py recall "Brownian carousel mistakes". The memory recall reported no carousel-specific memory. Math cards covered mostly unrelated results and the 2026 correlation paper.','Searched D0047 in intake directories and codex_pool_2026_10_10. Recovered D0047-A001 and six 2026-09-17 reports from origin/master of ~/math-open-problems using git show, saved locally as prior_*.md. The reports are hints, not independently certified proofs. No repository was changed.','Earlier work reduced a one-pole Lax family to sigma-PV conditional on selecting the physical solution. That selection remains unproved. Its claim that the small-gap intensity alone selects the PV branch is too weak: the exact exponential/linear-sigma branch in ATTEMPT.md has the same slope.','## Verdict','No paper was located stating and proving THIS question with the physical Brownian-carousel selection. Therefore SOLVED_IN_LITERATURE is not claimed.']
